OBS id=AGENTCMD-PROFILE-FAIL :: Integrated Windows acceptance exposed a concrete user-environment conflict: with only agentcmd.wc enabled, pane get correctly records the module directory, but the user's normal PowerShell profile prepends C:/Users/eda/AppData/Local/Programs/Agent Commands to PATH afterward; `Get-Command wc.exe` then selects the pre-existing global wc, not the enabled module. `powershell.exe -NoProfile` on a separate isolated socket correctly selects the module and `wc -w` returns 2. Both test sockets stopped cleanly. This is not an absence test: sort/cat may continue resolving from the existing system/profile.
